      "content": "You are touching on a very common point of confusion. Wind speed is a scalar, but velocity is a vector. If we say 'the wind is blowing at 20 km/h', that is a scalar because it only gives magnitude. To make it a vector, we must include direction, like '20 km/h North'. \n\nIf a quantity *must* have a direction to be fully described, is it a scalar or a vector?"
