      "content": "A light ray is refracted when it travels from air into water. Which ONE of the following combinations relating to the DIRECTION OF THE REFRACTED RAY and the SPEED OF THE LIGHT RAY is CORRECT?\n\nA) DIRECTION OF THE REFRACTED RAY: Towards the normal | SPEED OF THE LIGHT RAY: Decreases\nB) DIRECTION OF THE REFRACTED RAY: Away from the normal | SPEED OF THE LIGHT RAY: Decreases\nC) DIRECTION OF THE REFRACTED RAY: Towards the normal | SPEED OF THE LIGHT RAY: Increases\nD) DIRECTION OF THE REFRACTED RAY: Away from the normal | SPEED OF THE LIGHTRAY: Increases\n\nI think it's B because light speeds up when it enters water, right?"
