      "role": "assistant",
      "reasoning": "Student believes light speeds up in water and bends away from the normal (confident wrong). Use a real-world running/tarmac-to-sand analogy to check their assumption about light speed in denser media. [TOOL CHECK: calculator(expression=\"3e8 / 1.333\") -> 225000000]",
      "content": "Let's test that idea using a familiar South African scenario! 🏃‍♂️ Imagine you are running fast on a smooth tar road (representing air), and suddenly you have to run diagonally into thick beach sand or shallow water at Clifton beach (representing water).\n\nWhen your first foot hits the heavier medium (sand/water), does your speed increase or decrease?"
